SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Bon Bons ***\nMothe
 r Ginger's Bon Bons — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Fl
 esh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes *Dancers of Color m
 ay wear flesh-tone ballet shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Hig
 h Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Pink Hat\; Prop (BA provide
 s): Lollipop\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powder matching
  skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease with an eye 
 shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake l
 ashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn
 ’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\
 nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes
 .\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while c
 hanging to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Balle
 t Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no
  matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the 
 floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitti
 ng on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, c
 lean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-u
 p while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging ma
 ke-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray p
 erfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assig
 ned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage while 
 in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes fro
 m their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobb
 y pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• Retu
 rn all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and 
 all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack mar
 kers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain cost
 umes.
